      "comments": [
        {
          "author": "thomwiggers",
          "authorAssociation": "NONE",
          "body": "This whole paragraph text seems very \"why doesn't TLS just work for you\". If the traffic is so continuous, you can keep a TLS session alive; EKU solves the gap for rekeying.  Meanwhile if your log integrity is so important, you actually need synchronous acknowledgement of log entries to avoid truncation attacks. So using that as an argument actually weakens the argument that a CURRENT-approach works better imo.",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-09T09:25:20Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-09-09T09:25:33Z"
        }
      ],
